{
  "nodes": {
    "start": {
      "id": "start",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Decimal numbers can look different from ordinary whole numbers, but the book gives us a simple procedure for finding their H.C.F. and L.C.M.\\n\\nThe key idea is: make the decimal places equal, remove the decimal point, solve the whole-number problem, and then restore the decimal places.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "why_equal_places"
        }
      ]
    },
    "why_equal_places": {
      "id": "why_equal_places",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Why do we first make the same number of decimal places?\\n\\nSuppose the numbers are 0.63, 1.05 and 2.1.\\n\\nThe first two numbers have two decimal places, but 2.1 has only one.\\n\\nSo we write:\\n\\n0.63, 1.05, 2.10\\n\\nWe have not changed the value of 2.1. We have only written it with the same decimal-place length as the others.\\n\\nThink of it like putting three measuring sticks into the same unit before comparing or combining them. The numbers are now prepared in the same format.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "decimal_places_check"
        }
      ]
    },
    "decimal_places_check": {
      "id": "decimal_places_check",
      "type": "CHOICE",
      "input": {
        "type": "CHOICE",
        "options": [
          {
            "id": "a",
            "label": "0.63, 1.05, 2.1"
          },
          {
            "id": "b",
            "label": "0.63, 1.05, 2.01"
          },
          {
            "id": "c",
            "label": "0.63, 1.05, 2.10"
          },
          {
            "id": "d",
            "label": "0.630, 1.050, 2.1000"
          }
        ]
      },
      "content": {
        "text": "Which is the correctly equalized form of 0.63, 1.05 and 2.1?",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "condition": {
            "field": "isCorrect",
            "value": true,
            "operator": "EQUALS"
          },
          "targetNodeId": "decimal_places_remedy"
