        }
      }
    },
    "decimal_places_remedy": {
      "id": "decimal_places_remedy",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Let's count carefully.\\n\\n0.63 → 2 decimal places\\n1.05 → 2 decimal places\\n2.1 → 1 decimal place\\n\\nSo the common format uses 2 decimal places. Append one zero to 2.1:\\n\\n2.1 → 2.10\\n\\nTherefore:\\n\\n0.63, 1.05, 2.10",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "hcf_63_start"
        }
      ]
    },
    "hcf_63_start": {
      "id": "hcf_63_start",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Now apply the next step from the book.\\n\\nGiven:\\n0.63, 1.05 and 2.10\\n\\nRemove the decimal points and treat them as whole numbers:\\n\\n63, 105 and 210\\n\\nThen find the H.C.F. of these whole numbers.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "hcf_63_compute"
        }
      ]
    },
