    "hcf_63_remedy": {
      "id": "hcf_63_remedy",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Let's verify the common factor.\\n\\n63 = 21 × 3\\n105 = 21 × 5\\n210 = 21 × 10\\n\\nSo 21 divides all three numbers exactly. The book gives H.C.F. = 21.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "hcf_63_restore"
        }
      ]
    },
    "hcf_63_restore": {
      "id": "hcf_63_restore",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "We are not finished yet. This is the step students often skip.\\n\\nThe original numbers were written with 2 decimal places after equalization:\\n\\n0.63, 1.05, 2.10\\n\\nOur whole-number H.C.F. is 21. Restore the 2 decimal places:\\n\\n21 → 0.21\\n\\nTherefore:\\n\\nH.C.F. of 0.63, 1.05 and 2.1 = 0.21",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "hcf_63_restore_check"
        }
      ]
    },
